# Define Data Definitions

Generate data definitions that will be added and or changed. These may include but are not
limited to: GraphQL types, data structures, types, etc.

## Inputs

- A ticket, story, use case, or feature description with acceptance criteria.
- Any prior codebase research.
- A high-level design that defines the current state, future state, decisions made, etc.

## Instructions
- Write data definitions using the syntax of the codebase (GraphQL, Elixir, TypeScript, etc.).
- Use `diff` when the point is what changes and the surrounding shape already exists. Match the diff shape to the topic.
- Write data definitions (e.g. GraphQL types, DB schemas, etc.) ONLY. Do not write functions, classes, etc.
- Output the results using the report format below.
- Emit the report itself. Do not wrap it in a code fence: the first line of your reply is the opening `## Data Definitions`. The report's top heading is `##`, and every heading inside it is `###` or deeper.

## Workflow

- Read all the inputs FULLY.
- Generate data definitions that will be needed and or changed.
- Report the data definitions following the report format below.

## Report Format
```md
## Data Definitions

### <topic>
<data definition>

### <topic>
<data definition>

...
```
